# A wallpaper behind the desktop, saved for the next boot. The picture is a
# screenshot taken while a viewer window was open: once the viewer is
# closed, its title bar (blue, 3a6ea5, at 300,36: above the terminal,
# which covers 38..762 x 42..558 at 800x600) is still in the wallpaper.
# On the RAM disk: writing megabytes to the test's IDE disk is slow (see
# the BeeFS write speed note in the README); the HP checks the reboot.
@ai
$ ai control on
$ display mode 800x600
~ ^mode: 800x600
$ screenshot /screen.bmp
$ view /screen.bmp
$ sleep 1
$ screenshot /paper.bmp
@ctl keys {machine} "q"
$ sleep 1
@screenshot 800x600 pixels 300,36=a8d0f0
$ desktop wallpaper /paper.bmp
wallpaper: /paper.bmp (800 x 600, scaled to cover the screen; RAM disk: not kept after reboot)
@screenshot 800x600 pixels 300,36=3a6ea5 5,5=a8d0f0
$ cat /system/wallpaper
/paper.bmp
# Another size: the wallpaper is scaled again (by 1.28 for 1024x768, so
# the title bar is now at 384,40).
$ display mode 1024x768
~ ^mode: 1024x768
@screenshot 1024x768 pixels 384,40=3a6ea5
$ desktop wallpaper none
wallpaper: none, the plain color
@screenshot 1024x768 pixels 300,36=a8d0f0
$ desktop wallpaper /note.txt
desktop wallpaper /note.txt: no such file or directory
